              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পাহাড় — pāhāṛ — \"a mountain\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "পাহাড় (pāhāṛ) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from pāhāḍa, \"rock, hill\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 8141). CDIAL thinks it probably connected with Sanskrit pāṣāṇa, \"stone\"."
            }
          ]
        },
